  "statement": {
    "title": "torch.nn spatial modules accept iterable arguments with the wrong dimensionality",
    "body": "Spatial torch.nn APIs can accept kernel, stride, padding, output-size, or related iterables whose length does not match the operation's dimensions, deferring failure or producing confusing results. A one-item iterable must expand across dimensions, an exact-length iterable must be accepted, and every other length must raise immediately.",
